# Everyday Buddy — release signing config (Track D).
#
# SETUP (once per release machine — NEVER commit the real file):
#
#   1. Generate a keystore OUTSIDE the repo (so it can never be committed):
#
#      keytool -genkeypair -v `
#        -keystore C:\secure\everyday-buddy-release.keystore `
#        -alias everyday-buddy -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
#
#      (Back up the keystore + passwords somewhere safe. Losing them means a
#      NEW app id on the Play Store — updates under com.everydaybuddy stop.)
#
#   2. Copy THIS file to `android/key.properties` (same folder, no `.example`)
#      and fill in the four values below.
#
#   3. `flutter build apk --release --split-per-abi` (or appbundle).
#
# NOTES:
# - `storeFile` may be absolute (recommended, forward slashes) or relative to
#   the `android/` folder. Absolute keeps the keystore outside the repo.
# - When `android/key.properties` is ABSENT, release builds fall back to the
#   debug signing config so CI and local dev still build. That APK is NOT
#   shippable — Gradle prints no warning, so check your signing before upload.
# - `key.properties`, `*.keystore`, and `*.jks` are gitignored (see
#   `mobile/android/.gitignore` + repo-root `.gitignore`). Do NOT force-add.

storeFile=C:/secure/everyday-buddy-release.keystore
storePassword=CHANGE_ME_store_password
keyAlias=everyday-buddy
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME_key_password
